WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.625
Raw collection needs processing before reliable analysis.

00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:08.104
Start by assigning stable identifiers to sources and artifacts.

00:00:08.104 --> 00:00:16.847
Group material by information need, source category, date, entity, or event while preserving the link to the original record.

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:18.340
Deduplicate carefully.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:25.804
Multiple pages may repeat one original claim, and treating them as independent sources creates false confidence.

00:00:25.804 --> 00:00:30.283
Track the earliest known origin and relationships among copies.

00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:33.908
Preserve meaningful differences, corrections, and publication times.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:38.813
Use tags consistently for entities, locations, systems, organizations, and themes.

00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:44.144
Entity extraction can accelerate organization, but names and identifiers require verification.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:52.461
Similar names do not prove the same identity, and one online identifier may be reused, shared, or reassigned.

00:00:52.461 --> 00:00:55.660
Timelines reveal sequence, delay, and contradiction.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:01.845
Normalize time zones and distinguish publication time from event time and collection time.

00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:10.588
Relationship maps can show documented connections, but every edge should cite evidence and describe what the connection actually means.

00:01:10.588 --> 00:01:14.640
Separate facts, source claims, assumptions, and analytical judgments.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.545
A fact may be directly supported by a reliable record.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:23.170
A claim is what a source says.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.369
An assumption fills a working gap.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:28.715
A judgment interprets evidence.

00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:33.620
Keeping these categories visible prevents inference from becoming accidental fact.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.966
Maintain traceability through processing.

00:01:35.966 --> 00:01:43.003
Summaries, tables, translations, and visual maps should point back to source identifiers and preserved context.

00:01:43.003 --> 00:01:50.041
Processing is successful when it reduces noise and exposes gaps without erasing provenance or uncertainty.
